<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Module 7 Worksheet</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1e293b;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 40px auto;
    max-width: 800px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #0f172a;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #7b4fce;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  h2, h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #7b4fce;
    margin-top: 35px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-left: 4px solid #00c8ff;
    padding-left: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: #334155;
  }
  ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    padding-left: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  li {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .checkbox {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-family: monospace;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-right: 10px;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .instructions {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #475569;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .question {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .response-box {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px dashed #7b4fce;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    margin: 10px 0 25px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #475569;
  }
  .response-label {
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #7b4fce;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  .response-placeholder {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PlayIQ Module 7 Worksheet: Summaries, Questions, and Precision</h1>
<div class="instructions"><strong>Instructions:</strong> Complete this worksheet thoughtfully. Remember, PlayIQ is about using AI as a coach, not a crutch. Your goal is to become an independent learner!</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 1: 10-Line Summary System</h3>
<div class="question">1. (Short Response) Why is copying an entire page of notes usually a bad summary?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">2. (Multiple Choice) The 10-Line Summary System forces you to:</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Write as fast as you can.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Decide what actually matters.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Copy exactly what the teacher said.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Use big words to sound smart.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">3. (Prompt Improvement) You want to summarize your history notes. Write a prompt asking your AI Coach to help you create a 10-Line Summary, making sure to ask the AI to let *you* write the first version.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">4. (Teach-Back) Explain to a friend why spending 5 minutes on a short, structured outline saves 30 minutes of getting stuck while studying.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 2: Turn Notes Into Questions</h3>
<div class="question">5. (Short Response) Why are notes "not finished" until they can test you?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">6. (Multiple Choice) Turning your notes into questions changes your studying from:</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Active recall to passive reading.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Hard work to easy work.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Passive reading into active recall.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Writing into typing.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">7. (Scenario) You have a paragraph of notes about the planets. You ask the AI to turn it into 3 Easy, 3 Medium, and 2 Challenge questions. Which type of question is most likely to ask you to "compare and contrast" two planets?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">8. (Teach-Back) Explain how turning your notes into questions changes how your brain interacts with the material.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 3: Find Missing Links</h3>
<div class="question">9. (Short Response) What is a "missing link" in your understanding?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">10. (Classification) You know the definition of "gravity" and you know the definition of "orbit," but you don't understand how gravity *causes* an orbit. Is this a missing word, a missing step, or a missing connection?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">11. (Scenario) You are reviewing a summary and a set of questions with the AI. You ask the AI for 3 diagnostic questions to find any missing links. The AI realizes you don't know the historical background of an event. What type of missing link is this?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">12. (Teach-Back) Explain the difference between knowing the definitions of words and actually understanding the "missing link" connections between them.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 4: Precision Prompting</h3>
<div class="question">13. (Short Response) A vague prompt gives vague help. Why is it important to tell the AI its "role" (e.g., Act as my learning coach)?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">14. (Multiple Choice) Which of the following is NOT a part of the Precision Prompt Formula?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Role</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Task</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Limits</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A polite greeting</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">15. (Prompt Improvement) A student writes this weak prompt: "Help me study biology." Upgrade this to a precision prompt by adding a Role, Task, Topic, Limits, Format, and Effort Rule.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">16. (Classification) In your prompt, you write: "Do not give me the answers before I try to guess them." Which part of the Precision Prompt Formula is this? (Role, Task, Limits, Format, or Effort Rule)</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">17. (Scenario) You use a precision prompt, and the AI perfectly formats a quiz, waits for your answers, and coaches you when you get stuck. How is this different from what usually happens when people use a generic prompt?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">18. (Teach-Back) Explain to a friend why adding "Limits" and an "Effort Rule" to an AI prompt makes the AI a much better tutor.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
